[
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a proof in Mathlib that the Hadamard (entrywise) product of positive definite real matrices is positive definite? I have a proof via the Kronecker product reduction that I could contribute. Would Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Hadamard be the right place, or should it be a separate file?</p>",
        "id": 582278458,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael R Douglas",
        "timestamp": 1774655578
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"201575\">Michael R Douglas</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Schur.20product.20theorem.20.28Hadamard.20product.20preserves.20posdef.29/near/582278458\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Is there a proof in Mathlib that the Hadamard (entrywise) product of positive definite real matrices is positive definite? I have a proof via the Kronecker product reduction that I could contribute. Would Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Hadamard be the right place, or should it be a separate file?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Is the proof AI generated ? Just if so it may take a lot of effort to get it in</p>",
        "id": 582279212,
        "sender_full_name": "Yan Yablonovskiy 🇺🇦",
        "timestamp": 1774656253
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It is a mix of human and AI.   If it doesn't get accepted I won't worry about it.</p>",
        "id": 582279389,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael R Douglas",
        "timestamp": 1774656412
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"644391\">@loogle</span> open Matrix in (_ ⊙ _).PosDef</p>",
        "id": 582280348,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1774657273
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"shrug\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f937\" role=\"img\" title=\"shrug\">:shrug:</span> nothing found</p>",
        "id": 582280350,
        "sender_full_name": "loogle",
        "timestamp": 1774657275
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So at least the result is not in mathlib; it might be in an open PR</p>",
        "id": 582280356,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1774657283
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks.   Does the choice of file matter or should I just add it to Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Hadamard</p>",
        "id": 582280680,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael R Douglas",
        "timestamp": 1774657502
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It can be moved around in review</p>",
        "id": 582281299,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1774658116
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37297\">#37297</a>)</p>",
        "id": 582294334,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1774667568
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>As <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"197836\">@Jireh Loreaux</span>  has just identified, a similar result is in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36478\">#36478</a></p>",
        "id": 582298175,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1774672688
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That one is shorter, but I guess only proves PosSemiDef.  You can decide which one you prefer</p>",
        "id": 582298335,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael R Douglas",
        "timestamp": 1774672952
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Could you please generalize it to infinite matrices? It follows from the finite case by specializing to the support</p>",
        "id": 582308698,
        "sender_full_name": "Hampus Nyberg",
        "timestamp": 1774685119
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>See also the chat <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"144837\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/144837-PR-reviews/topic/.2336478.20Schur.27s.20product/with/582437164\">#PR reviews &gt; #36478 Schur's product</a>. A version for the infinite case is there.</p>",
        "id": 582437368,
        "sender_full_name": "Tjeerd Jan Heeringa",
        "timestamp": 1774815349
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Based on my comment in the other chat, you can create both infinite dimensional version by introducing the lemmata </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">submatrix_hadamard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊙</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">submatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">submatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊙</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">submatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hadamard_apply</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">submatrix_apply</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PosDef</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">submatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PosDef</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">he</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Injective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">submatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PosDef</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">hM</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">submatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hne</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mapDomain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finsupp</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mapDomain_injective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">he</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finsupp</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mapDomain_zero</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Finsupp</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sum_mapDomain_index</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add_mul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_add</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hM</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hne</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and then using </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PosSemidef</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hadamard'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PosSemidef</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hB</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PosSemidef</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊙</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PosSemidef</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">classical</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsHermitian</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">conjTranspose_hadamard</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hadamard_comm</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hA</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isHermitian</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                  </span><span class=\"n\">hB</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isHermitian</span><span class=\"o\">],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">support</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hAs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">submatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Subtype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Subtype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PosSemidef</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hA</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">submatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hBs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">submatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Subtype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Subtype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PosSemidef</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hB</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">submatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hHads</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hAs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hadamard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hBs</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"