    {
        "content": "<p>It's more general so in principle it's OK with me.  What I don't know is whether there is some even more general way to accomplish this, say a tactic or lemma that says \"a quadratic form property that holds on all finite submatrices holds on the full matrix with finitely-supported vectors.\"   But what you propose is OK.</p>",
        "id": 582568631,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael R Douglas",
        "timestamp": 1774878479
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't see an easy way to do this for all \"quadratic form properties\", but having that lemma for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.PosSemidef#doc\">docs#Matrix.PosSemidef</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.PosDef#doc\">docs#Matrix.PosDef</a> is definitely in order.</p>",
        "id": 582569627,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1774878734
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What if we expressed <code>Matrix.PosSemidef</code> as something like <code>Matrix.toBilinFinsupp.PosSemidef</code>; that is, define <code>PosSemidef</code> on all bilinear maps?</p>",
